  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "New Features:\n- configure stream tracking and retention\n  Default stream receivers to provider-position tracking so idempotent handlers do not accumulate a receipt for every outbox message. Enable OutboxIdentity mode through ConfigureMessageTracker globally or Tracker.Configure per grain to retain logical-message deduplication across republishing.\n  Add optional RetentionPeriod settings that expire checkpoints, receipts, and RPC sender entries using receiver acceptance time. Cleanup accompanies accepted messages and their persisted business changes, with no scheduled work. An earliest-expiry bound avoids full-state scans until an entry could expire. Each acceptance captures one settings snapshot, and journaling records actual cleanup for deterministic recovery.\n  Applications upgrading from automatic receipts can explicitly enable OutboxIdentity to preserve that behavior, or use EvictStreamReceipts to discard receipt history while retaining resume checkpoints. Automatic eviction is disabled by default. Set RetentionPeriod to null globally or per grain to retain manual eviction, and reapply per-grain overrides through state configuration hooks.",
